                  <provenance type="#s"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_285">Kirkham, Yorkshire,
                     Augustinian priory of Holy Trinity or Christ Church</orgName><p>There is a
                     Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card for this attribution, written by
                     Andrew G. Watson and crediting Michael Gullick for the information. The card is
                     dated 1993 and therefore postdates the Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                     Supplement (1987). The attribution appears to have been accidentally omitted
                     during MLGB3 (2010-2015). The evidence on the card is as follows: <q>Principal
                     scribe wrote British library Additional MS 38817 and Arundel MS
                     36.</q></p><p>Compare also Teresa Webber and Andrew G. Watson, <title>The
                     Libraries of the Augustinian Canons</title>, Corpus of British Medieval Library
                     Catalogues, 6 (London, 1998), p. 32: <q>Very little evidence survives for the
                     library of Kirkham [...] One more manuscript, BL MS Burney 216, may be assigned
                     to Kirkham since the hand of one of its scribes has been identified by Michael
                     Gullick in two Kirkham books, BL MS Add. 38817 and BL MSS Arundel
                     36.</q></p></provenance>
               </history>
